-- title:
--   Irreducibility of the level-ℓ modular equation at ̃ j_N
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $p$, $p$ a prime, let $N\ge 1$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$, $p\nmid N$ and $p\neq\ell$. Inside the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ put $\tilde j=\mathrm{jqModC}\,\kappa$, the product of the monomial $q^{-1}$ with the image in $\kappa[[q]]$ of the integral power series `jNum`, and $\tilde j_N=\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\kappa\,N$, obtained from $\tilde j$ by the exponent-scaling ring homomorphism `qExpand` that multiplies all exponents by $N$ (substitution $q\mapsto q^N$); let $\bar F_N=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,N$ be the intermediate field $\kappa(\tilde j,\tilde j_N)$ of $\kappa((q))/\kappa$ generated by these two elements, which contains $\tilde j_N$. Let $\mathrm{data}_\ell$ be a package of level-$\ell$ modular polynomial data: a polynomial $\Phi\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic in $Y$, of degree $\psi(\ell)=\sum_{d\mid \ell,\ d\ \text{squarefree}}\ell/d$ in $Y$, and satisfies $\Phi(j(q),j(q^{\ell}))=0$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$. The assertion is that the one-variable polynomial over $\bar F_N$ obtained from $\Phi$ by reducing its integer coefficients into $\bar F_N$ and substituting $\tilde j_N$ for the inner variable $X$, namely $\Phi(\tilde j_N,Y)\in\bar F_N[Y]$, is irreducible.
--
--   This is the classical irreducibility of the modular equation of prime level $\ell$ over the level-$N$ modular function field, here in characteristic $p$ with $p\nmid N\ell$; equivalently $\Phi_\ell(\tilde j_N,Y)$ is the minimal polynomial of $\tilde j_{N\ell}$ over $\kappa(\tilde j,\tilde j_N)$, so that this extension has degree $\ell+1$. It is used in the construction of the automorphisms of the modular function field that exchange the two distinguished generators, in [`ModularCurve.exists_algEquiv_modularFunctionFieldC_swap_and_charLDegeneracyRoof_swap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_algEquiv_modularFunctionFieldC_swap_and_charLDegeneracyRoof_swap).
